55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate A has proven clinical value, but my findings on visit completion and @Servas's point on tariffs make it a high risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate C requires a ""dedicated space,"" but our rooms are already full. Candidate B uses scheduled slots, which fits our booking system.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate B is joint-run, which is a red flag. Candidate D requires outside surgery agreements, which take forever. Candidate C is a standalone unit.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Candidate B is perfect because the midwifery team has slack! Candidate C is scary because physiotherapists are leaving for the city.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Candidate C requires fitting out floor space, which now comes out of our reduced development budget. That is a heavy cost.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"If C is too expensive and A is too unreliable, B or D are left. But D's reliance on outside data agreements is a logical dead end.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"B is on-site, meaning it generates tariffs and fits the booking system. The ""joint"" nature is a risk, but the physical logistics work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi's point about midwifery slack might mitigate the ""joint"" failure risk. If one side has capacity, they can carry the weight.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Yumi,,Yes! The midwives would be so happy to help. It's much better than adding to the ward nursing vacancies.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Servas,,A program that utilizes existing slack and generates revenue is a sustainable seed. Candidate B seems the most harmonious.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. While B is joint-run, the clinical need for perinatal support is steady, and it avoids the pitfalls of home visits and external data links.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It is the only one that doesn't threaten to seize up our parking or our booking screens.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It's a calculated risk. The staffing slack is the variable that makes B viable where other joint ventures failed.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for B! It's the kindest choice for the staff.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Servas,,"When we align the needs of the patient with the capacity of the provider, we find success. I support Candidate B.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will vote for B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Yumi,,B!,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Servas,,B.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
